Subject: [PATCH v1 0/4] media: qcom: camss: Galaxy A52 (SM7125) streaming fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A set of qcom-camss fixes found while bringing up the cameras on the
Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125):

1. Reset the per-output state on stream-off and never arm the VFE write
   master without a queued buffer, so a restart does not re-use stale
   addresses.
2. Take the CSIPHY/CSID lane count from the active sensor instead of the
   fixed DT lane map, so sensors that run fewer lanes in a given mode are
   programmed correctly.
3. VFE gen2: when only a single buffer is queued, point the double-buffered
   write master's pong slot at that same buffer instead of leaving it at the
   reset value 0 (which faults the SMMU as a write to IOVA 0). Mirrors the
   gen1 path.
4. CSIPHY 3ph: poll for the revision id on a cold power-up; the id latches
   with a propagation delay after the block is first clocked, so the
   immediate read returned 0.

Dependency / base: this series sits on top of the a52q camera stack rather
than on plain v7.3-rc5. Patch 2 adds a get_mbus_config op to the GC5035,
IMX616, S5K3L6XX and S5KGW1P sensor drivers, which are themselves pending
in separate media series; patches 1/3/4 touch the Gen2/C-PHY camss paths
from the camss-cphy and camss-sc7180 series. Base commit used for these
patches: v7.3-rc5 + media-camss-cphy + media-camss-sc7180 +
media-sensor-{gc5035,imx616,s5k3l6xx,s5kgw1p}.

Not independently tested on hardware by the submitter tooling; on-device
verification pending (the gen2 pong fix was validated against a logged
SMMU IOVA-0 fault but not re-streamed post-fix).

Miroslav Mráz (4):
  media: qcom: camss: reset output state and never arm WM without a
    buffer
  media: qcom: camss: take CSIPHY/CSID lane count from the active sensor
  media: qcom: camss: vfe-gen2: never arm the write master with a zero
    pong buffer
  media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: wait for the revision id on cold
    power-up

